      "note": "raw capture: the serialized DOM text exactly as returned by the reference public API, byte for byte. NOT byte-stable across runs: per DATA-MODEL R6.1 the [idx] value IS Chrome backendNodeId, a per-launch counter that drifts by a small constant offset (measured: +-1, uniform across every index on the page) depending on how many nodes the renderer allocated before the document. Structure, order, attributes and text are identical; only the integers move. Compare .normalized.txt instead."
    },
    {
      "applied": "selector indices [N] remapped to 1..N in first-appearance order",
      "artifact": "python-golden/<page>.normalized.txt",
      "byte_stable_across_runs": true,
      "comparison_target": true,
      "note": "THE parity comparison target. Removes Chrome per-launch id numbering while preserving index ASSIGNMENT ORDER, which is what R6.1/R6.2 actually constrain. Verified byte-identical across three full independent recording runs, 25/25 pages."
    },
    {
      "applied": "keys sorted, indent=2, LF endings; no id rewriting",
