    {
      "applied": "every 32-uppercase-hex token (frameId / loaderId / sessionId / targetId) replaced by <ID:n> in first-appearance order",
      "artifact": "cdp-input/<page>.json",
      "byte_stable_across_runs": false,
      "comparison_target": false,
      "note": "replay INPUT, never a comparison target. The hex-id normalization removes the per-launch UUID drift, but nodeId/backendNodeId integers inside the payloads still carry the same +-1 counter offset as the text. That is harmless: a replay consumer reads these ids relationally, it does not compare them to a constant."
    }
